; @ARCHIVE@ uninstall: removes what its Install put in. For an archive that needs
; the base, the base's Uninstall runs the copy of this script in @RECORD@ before it
; removes the base; a stand-alone archive is left alone by the base.
; Run from anywhere:  Execute Uninstall
FailAt 21
; UP-Term: can be a multi-directory assign, where Delete finds a path below the first directory only: the
; Delete lines name the one real drawer (UPTREAL:) the Install wrote to, as resolve-addon.dos assigns it
; @include dist/common/@RECORDRESOLVE@
; @include dist/addons/@ID@/uninstall-body.dos
; @include dist/common/@ADDONVAR@
; the record: its copy of this script is the one a base Uninstall is running, which
; AmigaDOS cannot delete while it is read (the base removes it with its own drawer)
Delete >NIL: "$uptrec" ALL QUIET
; the drawer of records goes too when this was the last (Delete without ALL: only an empty drawer)
Delete >NIL: "$uptpkg" QUIET
Assign >NIL: UPTREAL:
Echo "@ARCHIVE@ removed."
